{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unrelative-inbred-piglet","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Symptom\n\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ.py` fails with\n\n    AssertionError: assert False\n      where False = isinstance(Mutation(direction=..., action=..., target='DSO-42', ...),\n                               <class 'mutation.Mutation'>)\n\ni.e. an object that IS a `Mutation` fails `isinstance` against `Mutation`. Observed on\n`macos-latest / py3.13` in CI while `ubuntu-latest / py3.13` — same Python version — passed, which is the\nsignature of a collection-order dependency rather than a version or logic defect.\n\n## Root cause (reproduced deterministically, not inferred)\n\nFive test files load `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mutation.py` **by path** under the SHARED\n`sys.modules` key `\"mutation\"`:\n\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ.py`\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ_conflict_resolution.py`\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ_quarantine_suppression.py`\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ_emits_probe.py`\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_mutation.py`\n\nThree of them shared this helper:\n\n    def _load_module(name: str, path: Path) -> ModuleType:\n        spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(name, path)\n        mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n        sys.modules.setdefault(name, mod)   # keeps an EARLIER registration\n        spec.loader.exec_module(mod)\n        return mod                          # ...but returns the NEW module\n\n`setdefault` keeps whatever was registered first, yet the function returns the freshly-created module. So\nwhenever another file has already registered `\"mutation\"`, the fixture hands back a module object that is\n**not** `sys.modules[\"mutation\"]` — two live copies of the same source, with two distinct `Mutation` classes.\n\nMeanwhile `differ._load_mutation()` resolves its `Mutation` cache-first out of `sys.modules` (checking\n`\"mutation\"`, `\"rebar_reconciler.mutation\"`, …). So the differ builds objects from copy A while the test\nasserts against copy B, and `isinstance` is correctly `False`.\n\nWhichever file pytest collects first wins the `setdefault`, so the outcome depends on collection order —\nwhich differs between macOS and Linux.\n\n**Deterministic reproduction** (fails before the fix, passes after):\n\n    pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ_conflict_resolution.py \\\n           tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ.py -q\n\nThe natural alphabetical order puts `test_differ.py` first, so it normally wins and the suite is green; that\nis why this sat latent.\n\n## Fix (landed with story J4, `0a94-e104-7304-4d85`)\n\nMake the helper cache-first, so the returned module always IS the registered one — mirroring what\n`differ._load_mutation()` already does:\n\n    cached = sys.modules.get(name)\n    if cached is not None and getattr(cached, \"__file__\", None) == str(path):\n        return cached\n    ...\n    sys.modules[name] = mod\n\nApplied to the three `setdefault`-based helpers. `test_differ_emits_probe.py` already assigned\nunconditionally (self-consistent) and `test_mutation.py` loads inline, so neither carried the defect.\n\n## Why it was bundled with J4 rather than landed separately\n\nJ4 added two test files, which perturbed macOS collection order enough to make another registrant win the\nrace — turning a latent landmine into a `Verified -1` that blocked J4's own change. The fix therefore had to\nsit at or below J4 in the review stack for J4 to go green. It is test-only, ~6 lines across three files, and\nthe alternative (a separate change spliced beneath an already-pushed one, blocking on its own plan review)\nbought nothing. The bundling is disclosed in J4's commit message rather than smuggled.\n\n## Remaining work this ticket tracks\n\n- [ ] Consider a shared conftest helper so the by-path loader exists ONCE instead of being copy-pasted into\n      five test modules — the duplication is what let three copies carry the same defect\n- [ ] Audit the other shared by-path `sys.modules` keys (`differ`, `config`, `adf`, `outbound_fields`,\n      `comment_limits`) for the same `setdefault`-then-return-new shape\n- [ ] Consider making CI run the suite in a randomized order (e.g. `pytest-randomly`) so order-dependent\n      coupling fails fast and locally rather than as a platform-specific surprise","id":"2bc7-d77b-641c-42aa","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Test helpers return an unregistered copy of mutation.py, so isinstance fails on a collection-order flip"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785352804914422001,"uuid":"ee4fd2bb-676e-4950-882d-bc8634cf0c56"}